# start

(? get_quest("march") == 0) -> last_results
(? get_quest("march") == 1) -> find_house
(? get_quest("march") == 2) -> karo_note
(? get_quest("march") == 3) -> karo_hub
(? get_quest("march") == 4) -> read_book

# back

GO cdc.ska -> router

# last_results

cdc: "So our analysis of the overdose victim's body in Muldraugh revealed some critical information."

cdc: "Velvet is *definitely* involved with all of this somehow, but it wasn't enough to actually animate the bodies, or cause the aggression we've been seeing."

# intro

cdc: "We want you to investigate the military angle on this next one. The details are hazy, but we've made contact with some surviving leadership at the Cheyenne Mountain bunker in Colorado, and they're sharing information with us." 

cdc: "If you want some evidence that the world has ended, there it is. Jesus."

cdc: "Anyway. Their own records are pretty hazy. But they've sent us the address of their chief scientist on what they're calling Project Acorn."

cdc: "His name was Dr. Caleb Ashley. Immunologist, virologist, you name it."

cdc: "I actually attended a talk of his at a conference once ... you know. Before."

cdc: "Whatever the hell happened down there, he's directly involved. We're hoping if you can find his house in March Ridge, you can find some notes that will give us more information."

> I'm in.

~ set_quest("march", 1)

cdc: "Excellent."

cdc: "Oh, and bring a radio with you on this one. You might need to call in for further guidance from the field."

# find_house

cdc: "Any questions?"

> Anything specific I should bring?
  cdc: "You won't need any special equipment this time."
  cdc: "But we are recommending you bring a radio with you. We can pass on instructions from the military as needed, depending on what you find."
  -> find_house
> How do I find the house?
  cdc: "It's on the eastern corner of Bradley and Churchill. There's a hedge and a little shed out back. Can't miss it."
  -> find_house
> What's the deal with March Ridge?
  cdc: "It's a military town, almost all service personnel."
  cdc: "Not a base per se, just base housing."
  cdc: "We're actually not sure why the truck was coming out of there when it crashed -- there's no lab or secure facilities in town."
  -> find_house

--- SECTION: KARO'S NOTE

# karo_note

cdc: "Did you find something?"

> Dr. Ashley's body. And a note from a Lt. Karo. He took the notebook and was headed to someplace called "Forest Station."

cdc: "Ok. Give me a minute, I'm going to get in touch with Cheyenne Mountain."

A long pause ensues. You can hear activity in the background.

Then, a moment later, heated voices and swearing.

cdc: "{pc_first_name()}, you there?"

> Yes?

cdc: "Apparently there's a goddamn *secret research base* in your neck of the woods, buried in the forest west of Rosewood a few clicks."

> The fuck?!

cdc: "That's what I said!"

cdc: "Our contacts at Cheyenne just found out themselves, they've got a big old mainframe they keep querying every time I ask them a question."

cdc: "Lieutenant Karo was Ashley's assistant. Unfortunately, it seems like he never made it to Forest Station."

# note_hub

cdc: "Does the note say anything else?"

> (? !note_scratched) It says he got scratched.
  ~ note_scratched = true
  cdc: "Yikes. That's not good. For 99.9% of people, that means turning, and turning *fast*."
  -> note_hub
> (? !note_blood) There's blood on it.
  ~ note_blood = true
  cdc: "That doesn't seem like a good sign."
  -> note_hub
> It says he was going home to get his keys.
  -> note_keys

# note_keys

cdc: "Ah. Okay. Hold on."

More voices in the background, questions and answers.

cdc: "Okay. Karo lived in the March Ridge military apartments on Folger Street, north end of town, between the school and the movie theater."

cdc: "He was quartered in the northwestern corner apartment on the top floor, with a couple of other soldiers."

cdc: "Go check it out -- if we're lucky, the notebook is still there."

> I'm on it.

~ set_quest("march", 3)

cdc: "Good. Call us with what you find."

cdc: "Good luck out there."

cdc: "CDC, over and out."
EXIT

--- SECTION: KARO HUB

# karo_hub

cdc: "Have you managed to gain access to Karo's apartment?"

> (? has_item("AshleyNotebook")) Yes, and I have Dr. Ashley's notebook!
  -> got_notebook
> Where was it again?
  -> .check_loc
> Not quite.
  -> .not_yet

## check_loc

cdc: "It's on the top floor of the military apartments on Folger Street. Northwestern corner apartment."
cdc: "I'm guessing you haven't gotten in there yet?"

> (? has_item("AshleyNotebook")) Actually, yes I have, and I have Dr. Ashley's notebook!
  -> got_notebook
> Not quite.
  -> -not_yet

## not_yet

cdc: "No worries, {pc_first_name()}. We're wishing you luck!"

cdc: "CDC, over and out."

EXIT

# got_notebook  

cdc: "Hell yes!"

~ set_quest("march", 4)
-> read_book

# read_book

cdc: "Are you ready to read the book to us now, or do you need to wait until a better time?"

> I'm ready now.
  -> reading
> Another time might be better.
  cdc: "Understood. Can't wait! Give us a call when you're ready."
  cdc: "CDC, over and out."
  EXIT

# reading

cdc: "Great. Go ahead when ready."

You begin to read the book out loud, as Daniel and presumably the rest of the CDC listen attentively on the other end of the line.

It starts with what might have sounded horrifying, before the world ended: anthrax, spallpox, ebola, SARS.

Painfully mundane now.

You skim at Daniel's instruction until, suddenly, two-thirds of the way through the book, the first mention of the same overdose victim you just uncovered in Muldraugh.

Something was different with Velvet; not different like LSD or crack once had been, but *fundamentally*, *dangerously* different. 

So different that Dr. Ashley had not believed it was possible for a normal drug lab, even a cartel-run one, to manufacture on their own.

Ashley had taken the sample to study in Forest Station, which, it seems, was a deep-ground secret research based to the west of Rosewood.

Daniel breaks in at this point.

cdc: "For the record, {pc_first_name()}, I think that might be your next stop."

You keep reading. In addition to researching the drug at Forest Station, Ashley also worked with local law enforcement to trace the source.

A page before the abrupt end of the book, a clue. Ashley had found a name. Dr. Emilia Herrera. A disgraced academic who'd once worked at the Louisville State University before apparently suffering a mental break and just ... vanishing.

Ashley had found an address for her, in the the last place he'd expected: a trailer park on the outskirts of Muldraugh.

The notebook ends in spatters of blood. A page is missing; the note left in Ashley's home by Lt. Karo.

~ set_quest("march", 100)

Daniel is silent for a long time, absorbing everything.

> So now what?

cdc: "Let me run this past our friends in Cheyenne Mountain. When you get back to us, hopefully we'll have some next steps for you."

cdc: "It sounds to me though that we have two leads: the scientist and the military base."

cdc: "Impeccable work, {pc_first_name()}."

cdc: "Daniel Chidi, CDC, over and out."
EXIT
